<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Bastard Sword</h1>
<p>One or Two-handed
</p><p>Also called the Hand and a Half Sword. The Bastard Sword is a long, straight bladed weapon with a rather plain, undecorated grip. While the blade could be used for thrusting, most often the wielder would swing it like a baseball bat. Ordinarily the weapon could be wielded with one hand, but the grip was long enough to accommodate a two-handed grip when necessary. The blade length was rarely much longer than that of a simple long sword, but because the weapon could be used with two hands (although there was really just enough room on most grips for about one and a half hands), it really couldn't be categorized as either a one or two handed weapon, making it a bastard as far as swords go. The executioner's sword of the 16th century is a great example of the Bastard Sword design.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla there is no bastard sword skill of its own: such a weapon is fought with the skill of the kind of weapon it is. Look at it to see which (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>).
</p><p><br />
